{"full":"hf:zadid6pretam/GOTabPFN","spaceId":"zadid6pretam/GOTabPFN","name":"GOTabPFN","source":"huggingface","description":"ICML 2026 GOTabPFN demo for high-dimensional tabular data.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":4,"created":"2026-05-31T06:41:02.000Z","updated":"2026-07-20T20:34:51.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://zadid6pretam-gotabpfn.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/zadid6pretam/GOTabPFN","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:09.019Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:09.019Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:09.019Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["GOTabPFN: From Feature Ordering to Compact Tokenization for Tabular Foundation Models on High-Dimensional Data","GOTabPFN is designed for high-dimensional tabular datasets where standard TabPFN-style predictors become difficult to use directly due to large feature counts. It takes a raw feature matrix and labels, learns an ordered and compressed representation, and then performs prediction using a frozen TabPFN-2.5 head.","GOTabPFN is not limited to biomedical datasets. It can be applied to any high-dimensional tabular dataset with a compatible feature matrix and target labels, including biomedical, transcriptomic, text, sensor, and image-feature datasets."],"features":["GO-LR learns a global feature order Pi from cluster-wise feature graphs.","NSC segments the ordered feature axis and compresses each segment into a compact meta-feature.","TabPFN-2.5 performs prediction on the compressed token vector Z(x)."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/zadid6pretam/GOTabPFN/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ae7e64d00f81023e2a5af5b27568df22e1338d43a7ed5bed3220fe88a649e03","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:09.057Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:41:09.057Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"